---
const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="footer">
  <div class="w-wide footer-inner">
    <p class="footer-copy">© {currentYear} dstN. All rights reserved.</p>
    <div class="footer-links">
      <a href="/work/">Work</a>
      <button type="button" id="legal-trigger">Legal</button>
      <a href="https://github.com/dstN" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<!-- Legal Modal -->
<div class="modal-backdrop" id="legal-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="legal-title">
  <div class="modal-content">
    <div class="modal-header">
      <h2 id="legal-title">Legal Information</h2>
      <button class="modal-close" id="legal-close" aria-label="Close" type="button">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-body">
      <h3>Imprint</h3>
      <p class="legal-meta">Information according to § 5 DDG:</p>
      <p>Dustin Tramm<br/>c/o Impressumservice Dein-Impressum<br/>Stettiner Str. 41<br/>35410 Hungen<br/>Germany</p>
      <p>Email: <a href="#" id="legal-email" data-u="dustin.tramm" data-d="yinside.de">dustin.tramm [at] yinside.de</a></p>
      <a href="/#contact" id="legal-contact-link" class="legal-cta">Open contact form</a>

      <h3>Privacy Policy</h3>
      <p>This website is designed with privacy in mind. It is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages. I do not use cookies, tracking scripts, or analytics services, and I collect no personal data myself while you browse. What GitHub logs when you open a page, and what happens when you send the contact form, is described below.</p>

      <h4>Controller</h4>
      <p>The controller for this website under the GDPR is Dustin Tramm, at the address and email given in the imprint above.</p>

      <h4>Hosting &amp; Server Logs</h4>
      <p>This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St., San Francisco, CA 94107, United States. When you open a page, GitHub logs your IP address for security purposes, whether or not you are signed in to GitHub. According to its privacy statement, GitHub also records data about each request automatically, such as device information and the date and time of the request. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in delivering this site securely and reliably (Art. 6 (1) f GDPR).</p>
      <p>This data is processed in the USA. GitHub, Inc. is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, so the transfer is based on the European Commission's adequacy decision of 10 July 2023 (Art. 45 GDPR). GitHub does not say how long it keeps the logs of GitHub Pages. Details are in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/about-github-pages#data-collection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's notes on data collection for GitHub Pages</a> and in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>

      <h4>Contact Form</h4>
      <p>When you send the contact form, your name, email address and message travel encrypted to a script under contact.yinside.de on my webspace at netcup GmbH, Emmy-Noether-Straße 10, 76131 Karlsruhe, Germany. netcup processes the data on my behalf under a data processing agreement (Art. 28 GDPR). Its servers are in Germany; for this part, no data is transferred to a third country. The script stores nothing: it forwards your message at once by email to my mailbox dustin.tramm [at] yinside.de, which is also hosted by netcup.</p>
      <p>The web server of contact.yinside.de writes access and error logs with your IP address, the time, the requested file, the page the request comes from and your browser. They are deleted after 3 days at the latest.</p>
      <p>If you write to me about a project, the legal basis is Art. 6 (1) b GDPR (steps prior to a contract, at your request); for any other message it is my legitimate interest in answering it (Art. 6 (1) f GDPR). I delete your message once your request is done, unless tax or commercial law requires me to keep it.</p>

      <h4>Local Storage</h4>
      <p>This site uses your browser's localStorage to remember your theme preference (light/dark mode). This data is stored only on your device and is never transmitted to any server.</p>

      <h4>Fonts</h4>
      <p>All fonts are self-hosted on this server. No requests are made to external font services (such as Google Fonts CDN). This ensures GDPR compliance for font delivery.</p>

      <h4>External Links</h4>
      <p>This site contains links to external websites (GitHub, LinkedIn, etc.). We are not responsible for the privacy practices of these sites.</p>

      <h4>Your Rights</h4>
      <p>You have the right to access the personal data I hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR), to have it corrected (Art. 16) or erased (Art. 17), to restrict its processing (Art. 18), to receive it in a portable format (Art. 20), and not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated processing (Art. 22); this site makes no such decisions. To use these rights, contact me via the email above.</p>
      <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), in particular in the Member State of your habitual residence, place of work or place of the alleged infringement.</p>

      <h4>Right to Object</h4>
      <p>Where I process your data on the basis of legitimate interests (Art. 6 (1) f GDPR), you have the right to object at any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation (Art. 21 (1) GDPR). I will then no longer process the data unless I can demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests, rights and freedoms, or the processing serves to establish, exercise or defend legal claims. An email to the address above is enough.</p>

      <p>Last updated: 30 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  const trigger = document.getElementById("legal-trigger")!;
  const modal = document.getElementById("legal-modal")!;
  const closeBtn = document.getElementById("legal-close")!;

  function openModal() {
    modal.classList.add("open");
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
    closeBtn.focus();
  }

  function closeModal() {
    modal.classList.remove("open");
    document.body.style.overflow = "";
    trigger.focus();
  }

  trigger.addEventListener("click", openModal);
  closeBtn.addEventListener("click", closeModal);

  // Close on backdrop click
  modal.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    if (e.target === modal) closeModal();
  });

  // Close on Escape
  document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
    if (e.key === "Escape" && modal.classList.contains("open")) closeModal();
  });

  // Email obfuscation
  const legalEmail = document.getElementById("legal-email");
  if (legalEmail) {
    const u = legalEmail.dataset.u;
    const d = legalEmail.dataset.d;
    const email = `${u}@${d}`;
    legalEmail.setAttribute("href", `mailto:${email}`);
    legalEmail.textContent = email;
  }

  // "Open contact form" — close modal, scroll to contact
  const contactLink = document.getElementById("legal-contact-link");
  if (contactLink) {
    contactLink.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      closeModal();
      document.getElementById("contact")?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth" });
    });
  }
</script>
